# Build output.
/dist/
/vesper
/vesper.exe
*.exe
*.test

# Captures. A screenshot taken to check something is evidence for one
# afternoon, not an asset.
/shot.png
/*.png

# Saves.
*.save.json

# A model export that failed its check. build.sh leaves it there on purpose so
# it can be looked at, rather than deleting the evidence of what went wrong.
assets/models-src/.staging-*.glb

# go-task's up-to-date cache.
/.task/

# Asset backups.
#
# These were the only safety net before this repository existed: a directory
# copied aside by hand before each risky re-export. Git is that net now, and
# keeping them tracked as well would mean carrying several copies of every
# model through LFS forever.
#
# They are ignored rather than deleted. If you are reading this in a fresh
# clone and there are none, that is correct - the history has them.
# Anywhere under assets/, at any depth: these are hand-made safety copies from
# before this repository existed, and git is that safety net now.
assets/**/_backup-*/
assets/**/backup-*/
assets/_backup-*/
assets/backup-*/
